{"path":"numeric/math/erf","title":"erf, erff, erfl","titleHtml":"erf, erff, erfl","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/c/numeric/math/erf","section":"numeric","kind":"page","summary":"Errors are reported as specified in math_errhandling.","html":"<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc-header\">\n<td> <div>Defined in header <code><a href=\"/w/c/numeric/math\"><code>&lt;math.h&gt;</code></a></code>\n </div></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-c99\" id=\"Version_1\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\"><span class=\"kw4\">float</span> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; erff<span class=\"br0\">(</span> <span class=\"kw4\">float</span> arg <span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td> (1) </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-c99\">(since C99)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-c99\" id=\"Version_2\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\"><span class=\"kw4\">double</span> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;erf<span class=\"br0\">(</span> <span class=\"kw4\">double</span> arg <span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td> (2) </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-c99\">(since C99)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-c99\" id=\"Version_3\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\"><span class=\"kw4\">long</span> <span class=\"kw4\">double</span> erfl<span class=\"br0\">(</span> <span class=\"kw4\">long</span> <span class=\"kw4\">double</span> arg <span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td> (3) </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-c99\">(since C99)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc-header\">\n<td> <div>Defined in header <code><a href=\"/w/c/numeric/tgmath\"><code>&lt;tgmath.h&gt;</code></a></code>\n </div></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-c99\" id=\"Version_4\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\"><span class=\"co2\">#define erf( arg )</span></span></div></td>\n<td> (4) </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-c99\">(since C99)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<div class=\"t-li1\"><span class=\"t-li\">1-3)</span> Computes the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Error_function\" class=\"extiw\" data-external=\"1\">error function</a> of <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\">arg</span></code>.</div>\n<div class=\"t-li1\"><span class=\"t-li\">4)</span> Type-generic macro: If <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\">arg</span></code> has type <span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\"><span class=\"kw4\">long</span> <span class=\"kw4\">double</span></span>, <code>erfl</code> is called. Otherwise, if <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\">arg</span></code> has integer type or the type <span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\"><span class=\"kw4\">double</span></span>, <code>erf</code> is called. Otherwise, <code>erff</code> is called.</div>\n<h3 id=\"Parameters\">Parameters</h3>\n<table class=\"t-par-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-par\">\n<td> arg\n</td>\n<td> -\n</td>\n<td> floating-point value\n</td></tr></table>\n<h3 id=\"Return_value\">Return value</h3>\nIf no errors occur, value of the error function of <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\">arg</span></code>, that is <span class=\"mjax-fallback texhtml\" data-tex=\"\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{\\pi} }\\int_{0}^{arg}{e^{-{t^2} }\\mathsf{d}t}\"><span class=\"t-mfrac\"><table><tr><td>2</td></tr><tr><td><span class=\"t-mrad\"><span>√</span><span>π</span></span></td></tr></table></span><span>∫</span><span class=\"t-su t-su-b\">arg<br>0</span><i>e</i><sup>-t<span class=\"t-su\">2<br></span></sup>d<i>t</i></span>, is returned.\nIf a range error occurs due to underflow, the correct result (after rounding), that is <span class=\"mjax-fallback texhtml\" data-tex=\"\\frac{2\\cdot arg}{\\sqrt{\\pi} }\"><span class=\"t-mfrac\"><table><tr><td>2*arg</td></tr><tr><td><span class=\"t-mrad\"><span>√</span><span>π</span></span></td></tr></table></span></span>, is returned.\n<h3 id=\"Error_handling\">Error handling</h3>\n<p>Errors are reported as specified in <a href=\"/w/c/numeric/math/math_errhandling\"><code>math_errhandling</code></a>.\n</p><p>If the implementation supports IEEE floating-point arithmetic (IEC 60559),\n</p>\n<ul><li> If the argument is ±0, ±0 is returned\n</li><li> If the argument is ±∞, ±1 is returned\n</li><li> If the argument is NaN, NaN is returned\n</li></ul>\n<h3 id=\"Notes\">Notes</h3>\n<p>Underflow is guaranteed if <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\"><span class=\"sy3\">|</span>arg<span class=\"sy3\">|</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span> <a href=\"/w/c/types/limits\"><span class=\"kw375\">DBL_MIN</span></a><span class=\"sy2\">*</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><a href=\"/w/c/numeric/math/sqrt\"><span class=\"kw665\">sqrt</span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span>π<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy2\">/</span><span class=\"nu0\">2</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code>.\n</p>\n<span class=\"mjax-fallback texhtml\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{erf}(\\frac{x}{\\sigma \\sqrt{2} })\">erf(<span class=\"t-mfrac\"><table><tr><td>x</td></tr><tr><td>σ<span class=\"t-mrad\"><span>√</span><span>2</span></span></td></tr></table></span>)</span> is the probability that a measurement whose errors are subject to a normal distribution with standard deviation <span class=\"mjax-fallback texhtml\" data-tex=\"\\sigma\">σ</span> is less than <span class=\"mjax-fallback texhtml\" data-tex=\"x\">x</span> away from the mean value.\n<h3 id=\"Example\">Example</h3>\n<div class=\"t-example\">\n<pre data-lang=\"c\"><code><span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;math.h&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;stdio.h&gt;</span>\n&nbsp;\n<span class=\"kw4\">double</span> phi<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"kw4\">double</span> x1, <span class=\"kw4\">double</span> x2<span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n    <span class=\"kw1\">return</span> <span class=\"br0\">(</span>erf<span class=\"br0\">(</span>x2 <span class=\"sy2\">/</span> <a href=\"/w/c/numeric/math/sqrt\"><span class=\"kw665\">sqrt</span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"nu0\">2</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy2\">-</span> erf<span class=\"br0\">(</span>x1 <span class=\"sy2\">/</span> <a href=\"/w/c/numeric/math/sqrt\"><span class=\"kw665\">sqrt</span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"nu0\">2</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy2\">/</span> <span class=\"nu0\">2</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">}</span>\n&nbsp;\n<span class=\"kw4\">int</span> main<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"kw4\">void</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/c/io/puts\"><span class=\"kw835\">puts</span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"st0\">\"normal variate probabilities:\"</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <span class=\"kw1\">for</span> <span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"kw4\">int</span> n <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> <span class=\"sy2\">-</span><span class=\"nu0\">4</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span> n <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span> <span class=\"nu0\">4</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span> <span class=\"sy2\">++</span>n<span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n        <a href=\"/w/c/io/fprintf\"><span class=\"kw850\">printf</span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"st0\">\"[%2d:%2d]:&nbsp;%5.2f%%<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>\"</span>, n, n <span class=\"sy2\">+</span> <span class=\"nu0\">1</span>, <span class=\"nu0\">100</span> <span class=\"sy2\">*</span> phi<span class=\"br0\">(</span>n, n <span class=\"sy2\">+</span> <span class=\"nu0\">1</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n&nbsp;\n    <a href=\"/w/c/io/puts\"><span class=\"kw835\">puts</span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"st0\">\"special values:\"</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/c/io/fprintf\"><span class=\"kw850\">printf</span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"st0\">\"erf(-0) =&nbsp;%f<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>\"</span>, erf<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"sy2\">-</span><span class=\"nu16\">0.0</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/c/io/fprintf\"><span class=\"kw850\">printf</span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"st0\">\"erf(Inf) =&nbsp;%f<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>\"</span>, erf<span class=\"br0\">(</span>INFINITY<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">}</span></code></pre>\n<p>Output:\n</p>\n<pre data-output=\"1\"><code>normal variate probabilities:\n[-4:-3]:  0.13%\n[-3:-2]:  2.14%\n[-2:-1]: 13.59%\n[-1: 0]: 34.13%\n[ 0: 1]: 34.13%\n[ 1: 2]: 13.59%\n[ 2: 3]:  2.14%\n[ 3: 4]:  0.13%\nspecial values:\nerf(-0) = -0.000000\nerf(Inf) = 1.000000</code></pre> \n</div>\n<h3 id=\"References\">References</h3>\n<div class=\"t-ref-std-11\">\n<ul><li> C11 standard (ISO/IEC 9899:2011): \n</li></ul>\n<dl><dd><ul><li> 7.12.8.1 The erf functions (p: 249)\n</li></ul>\n</dd></dl>\n<dl><dd><ul><li> 7.25 Type-generic math &lt;tgmath.h&gt; (p: 373-375)\n</li></ul>\n</dd></dl>\n<dl><dd><ul><li> F.10.5.1 The erf functions (p: 525)\n</li></ul>\n</dd></dl>\n</div>\n<div class=\"t-ref-std-c99\">\n<ul><li> C99 standard (ISO/IEC 9899:1999): \n</li></ul>\n<dl><dd><ul><li> 7.12.8.1 The erf functions (p: 230)\n</li></ul>\n</dd></dl>\n<dl><dd><ul><li> 7.22 Type-generic math &lt;tgmath.h&gt; (p: 335-337)\n</li></ul>\n</dd></dl>\n<dl><dd><ul><li> F.9.5.1 The erf functions (p: 462)\n</li></ul>\n</dd></dl>\n</div>\n<h3 id=\"See_also\">See also</h3>\n<table class=\"t-dsc-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/c/numeric/math/erfc\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>erfc</span><span>erfcf</span><span>erfcl</span></span></a></div><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-c99\">(C99)</span></span><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-c99\">(C99)</span></span><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-c99\">(C99)</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>   computes complementary error function  <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(function)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td colspan=\"2\"> <div class=\"t-dsc-see\"><span><a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/math/erf\">C++ documentation</a></span> for <span class=\"t-dsc-see-tt\"><span>erf</span></span></div>\n</td></tr>\n</table>\n<h3 id=\"External_links\">External links</h3>\n<table>\n<tr>\n<td><a class=\"external text\" href=\"https://mathworld.wolfram.com/Erf.html\" data-external=\"1\">Weisstein, Eric W. \"Erf.\"</a> From MathWorld — A Wolfram Web Resource.\n</td></tr></table>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Parameters","id":"Parameters"},{"depth":3,"text":"Return value","id":"Return_value"},{"depth":3,"text":"Error handling","id":"Error_handling"},{"depth":3,"text":"Notes","id":"Notes"},{"depth":3,"text":"Example","id":"Example"},{"depth":3,"text":"References","id":"References"},{"depth":3,"text":"See also","id":"See_also"},{"depth":3,"text":"External links","id":"External_links"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C reference"},{"path":"numeric","title":"Numerics"},{"path":"numeric/math","title":"Common mathematical functions"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"erf, erff, erfl","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"4 declarations. Computes the error function of arg."},{"label":"Parameters","note":"arg"},{"label":"Return value","note":"If no errors occur, value of the error function of"},{"label":"Error handling","note":"Errors are reported as specified in math_errhandling."},{"label":"Notes","note":"Underflow is guaranteed if |arg| < DBL_MIN*(sqrt(π)/2)."},{"label":"Example"},{"label":"See also","children":[{"label":"erfc, erfcf, erfcl","note":"computes complementary error function"}]}]},"standards":["C99"],"wordCount":363,"codeBlockCount":2}
